    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d325">

                <pb facs="0361" n="357" sameAs="frus:frus1939v03/pg357"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">693.001/502: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-02-01T17:00:00+08:00">February 1, 1939—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 6:55 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Reference my January 31, 6 p.m. to Hankow<anchor n="78" xml:id="d325-f1"/> and
                    Tokyo’s No. 52, January 31, noon, concerning return of Americans to Hankow.</p>
                <p>In a conversation this morning the local Japanese Consul General confirmed that
                    the transport was the <hi rendition="#italic">Shinyo Maru</hi> and that it
                    carried to Hankow a party of foreigners. He stated that any information to the
                    contrary obtained in Tokyo must have been due to a misunderstanding.</p>
                <p>The essentials are that American business interests are unable to send their
                    representatives to Hankow (and other Yangtze ports) because of Japanese
                    restriction and that American interests are suffering therefrom.</p>
                <p>Sent to Tokyo. Repeated Department, Peiping, and Hankow.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
